{
  "description": "Remote browser tab CLIENT reducer (viewer side; plans/cmux-next/remote-tab-protocol.md, remote-tab-r2 client cx-wb5.29). Each case starts with no open menu or dialog and screen seq 0. After each step the reducer returns exactly these effects (in order) and note, or this reject (state unchanged); then the open menu token, open dialog token (null = none) and the last sent screen seq. Effects: send (a control message to the host), show_menu/close_menu, show_dialog/close_dialog (sheets), set_cursor, page, text_input, screen_applied, session. The viewer never answers a token that is not open, never acts on viewer-to-host messages, and closes open UI when the session crashes or closes. Implementation: cmux-tui/crates/cmux-remote-browser (client.rs).",
  "version": 1,
  "cases": [
